{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480612-why-were-there-only-two-books-published-for-dark-ages-mage","id":1480612,"title":"Why were there only two books published for Dark Ages: Mage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-09T18:51:41-07:00","id":1480612,"title":"Why were there only two books published for Dark Ages: Mage?","content":"Many of you are already familiar with Dark Ages: Mage, so I wont go over it. If you don't know what it is, a quick google search will suffice.<br /> <br /> The two books published for DA:M were its rulebook and DA:M grimoire, which was its source book. It makes no sense to me why there were so few books published for DA:M. Not only was it really simple to understand, it was also extremely fun to read. Foundations seemed like a great replacement for Paradigms, and had mechanical benefits. Pillar magick was a lot more interesting than sphere magick and seemed super fun to play. Fellowships were a lot more interesting to learn about than the traditions, technocracy, and crafts from M:TA. The setting had a high fantasy feel to it, with a dash of gritty realism that is inherent in all WOD game lines. This in itself would have made it perfect for a champaign about wizards and magic in the dark ages.<br /> <br /> So why weren't there more books published? From what I have seen on the forums, many of you seem to have enjoyed it. Ars Magica had like 10 books, and I consider it pretty boring compared to DA:M. Dark ages vampire was pretty popular, with people still talking about it to this day. So there was clearly a demographic which the company could have profited off of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 05-09-2022, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T19:28:07-07:00","id":1480615,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's the sense that the future is already written and Dark Ages Mystics are fated to be steamrolled by the Order of Reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T02:27:58-07:00","id":1480642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480612-why-were-there-only-two-books-published-for-dark-ages-mage?p=1480615#post1480615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's the sense that the future is already written and Dark Ages Mystics are fated to be steamrolled by the Order of Reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire the dark ages had a pretty similar theme, but they still published like more than a dozen books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 05-10-2022, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T02:45:58-07:00","id":1480645,"title":"","content":"I think they were thinking of ending the old WoD by then and didn't want to invest more resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T02:46:12-07:00","id":1480646,"title":"","content":"The basic answer is simple:<br /> <br /> The cWoD's original run was canceled. We have no idea what would have happened if the Revised era longer and more published books.<br /> <br /> Though really... eh? DA Mage got more books than some of the other games (and even one more book that some of the ones that got a DA book). A lot of the &quot;vampire&quot; books have plenty of material useful to DA games in general. DAV was also updating a lot of material from VDA for 2e, which didn't have books for any other game but WtA (and that wasn't exactly as useful as the DA version). <br /> <br /> The comparison to Ars Magica doesn't even make sense. AM predated the cWoD let alone the DA settings. It's its own game with its own fans.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T08:50:21-07:00","id":1480664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480612-why-were-there-only-two-books-published-for-dark-ages-mage?p=1480646#post1480646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basic answer is simple:<br /> <br /> The cWoD's original run was canceled. We have no idea what would have happened if the Revised era longer and more published books.<br /> <br /> Though really... eh? DA Mage got more books than some of the other games (and even one more book that some of the ones that got a DA book). A lot of the &quot;vampire&quot; books have plenty of material useful to DA games in general. DAV was also updating a lot of material from VDA for 2e, which didn't have books for any other game but WtA (and that wasn't exactly as useful as the DA version).<br /> <br /> The comparison to Ars Magica doesn't even make sense. AM predated the cWoD let alone the DA settings. It's its own game with its own fans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why was there a cancellation?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T08:50:21-07:00","id":1480665,"title":"","content":"deleted for double posting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T09:09:30-07:00","id":1480666,"title":"","content":"They canceled all the old WoD lines sometime in the early 2000s cause they wanted to make room for a new World of Darkness (the Chronicles of Darkness universe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T11:43:19-07:00","id":1480680,"title":"","content":"There was never really supposed to be a Dark Ages: Mage. The original idea was that each splat would get an historical setting with which to play. Vampire got Dark Ages, Werewolf had the Wild West, Wraith received World War 1, and Mage initially had The Sorcerer's Crusade. Changeling had a proposed setting, but I cannot recall what time-frame was pitched. Vampire: the Dark Ages sold so well that White Wolf expanded the line, thus the title flip to Dark Ages: insert splat. Later, Victorian Age Vampire was published, as the Dark ages became its own line.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T11:57:15-07:00","id":1480683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That isn't actually why but you do you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What was the actual reason then?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T13:08:36-07:00","id":1480686,"title":"","content":"The actual reason was complicated.<br /> <br /> First off, the games were showing their age. After over a decade, the systems and the settings had grown Byzantine to the point of turning off new players as the early 00s saw a movement away from big systems and big settings for anything that wasn't high fantasy. As well, the teams working on the WoD were growing to hate the games they loved because fixing the problems kept getting to the point of needing such a massive rebuild that you'd need to reboot things to do it. The WW bosses insisted each game line was it's own independent domain, so each head developer came up with their own solutions, while the fans were begging for more consistency and were instead getting the exact opposite. According to a lot of the WW people at the time, things had just gotten to that point: the current iteration of the WoD had to end for the line to progress. I think this is TyrannicalRabbit's bigger source of objection. The decision to end the original WoD came first. The idea to do a new WoD that went in a different but similar direction instead of a more straight up reboot came second.<br /> <br /> Second, the economy of RPGs in that time period was bleak. The OGL Boom was in full force, but the signs of the impending bust were obvious (WW has taking part in the boom, so they were in a great position to see how bad conditions were). The general economy was also killing the small brick and mortar stores that defined gaming in the 80s and 90s. Big stores carried some RPGs, but didn't have the atmosphere to encourage gaming groups. More stuff was going on-line. The conditions that fuels the supplement treadmill era were on the brink of collapse. So WW had to pick between ending the original WoD while there was time, or trying to end it a few years later after the whole RPG marketplace shat itself.<br /> <br /> Finally? The audience was aging. While in the early 00s WW was still a big enough brand to attract a significant number of new and young players (nothing like being the &quot;mature&quot; brand to get youth to buy your stuff), in general RPGs were facing an issue of a lot of people that were playing these games in highschool or college suddenly having jobs, and families, and all that annoying adult stuff eating up their time. This created a big division between the old schoolers that wanted their (doomed by circumstances) familiar way of doing things, and new schoolers that wanted to see things adapt in the hopes of keeping their fun but in a way that better suited where they were then instead of a decade previous.<br /> <br /> Basically, the WoD as it existed in 2003 was obviously at the end of it's practical lifespan as a product (not necessarily a brand, there's a reason the later revival worked and not trying during the second half of the 00s is a big part of that). WW chose to pick the ending they wanted and start something new rather than leave even more hanging than they did when the market would have killed the WoD anyway (keep in mind that despite their popularity Changeling and Wraith had already been cancelled previously for lack of sales).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T15:44:28-07:00","id":1480698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480612-why-were-there-only-two-books-published-for-dark-ages-mage?p=1480686#post1480686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The actual reason was complicated.<br /> <br /> First off, the games were showing their age. After over a decade, the systems and the settings had grown Byzantine to the point of turning off new players as the early 00s saw a movement away from big systems and big settings for anything that wasn't high fantasy. As well, the teams working on the WoD were growing to hate the games they loved because fixing the problems kept getting to the point of needing such a massive rebuild that you'd need to reboot things to do it. The WW bosses insisted each game line was it's own independent domain, so each head developer came up with their own solutions, while the fans were begging for more consistency and were instead getting the exact opposite. According to a lot of the WW people at the time, things had just gotten to that point: the current iteration of the WoD had to end for the line to progress. I think this is TyrannicalRabbit's bigger source of objection. The decision to end the original WoD came first. The idea to do a new WoD that went in a different but similar direction instead of a more straight up reboot came second.<br /> <br /> Second, the economy of RPGs in that time period was bleak. The OGL Boom was in full force, but the signs of the impending bust were obvious (WW has taking part in the boom, so they were in a great position to see how bad conditions were). The general economy was also killing the small brick and mortar stores that defined gaming in the 80s and 90s. Big stores carried some RPGs, but didn't have the atmosphere to encourage gaming groups. More stuff was going on-line. The conditions that fuels the supplement treadmill era were on the brink of collapse. So WW had to pick between ending the original WoD while there was time, or trying to end it a few years later after the whole RPG marketplace shat itself.<br /> <br /> Finally? The audience was aging. While in the early 00s WW was still a big enough brand to attract a significant number of new and young players (nothing like being the &quot;mature&quot; brand to get youth to buy your stuff), in general RPGs were facing an issue of a lot of people that were playing these games in highschool or college suddenly having jobs, and families, and all that annoying adult stuff eating up their time. This created a big division between the old schoolers that wanted their (doomed by circumstances) familiar way of doing things, and new schoolers that wanted to see things adapt in the hopes of keeping their fun but in a way that better suited where they were then instead of a decade previous.<br /> <br /> Basically, the WoD as it existed in 2003 was obviously at the end of it's practical lifespan as a product (not necessarily a brand, there's a reason the later revival worked and not trying during the second half of the 00s is a big part of that). WW chose to pick the ending they wanted and start something new rather than leave even more hanging than they did when the market would have killed the WoD anyway (keep in mind that despite their popularity Changeling and Wraith had already been cancelled previously for lack of sales).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whoa, didn't know about all this. Its kind of sad when you think about how these games may never be as popular as they once were, feels like a slow death. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 05-10-2022, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T16:31:36-07:00","id":1480700,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of V5 (or things I've heard about W5 and H5) but the WoD is not dying because I don't like an edition, and the RPG market conditions aren't what they were like during the Clinton economic boom (again, economics far beyond RPGs matter, the 90s were so big for niche luxury items aimed at relatively low price points because it was boom economy for the middle class that has never truly been recovered from after multiple globally impacting economic disasters over the last two decades). <br /> <br /> V5 isn't going to reclaim VtM's position as the second biggest RPG. The WoD brand is, however, in general, the best it's been in a long time. The new reality of the RPG market is, once you stop trying to be a D&amp;D killer or caring what D&amp;D can do with Hasbro's monetary backing, currently pretty good and lots of older games are getting revisits by people that haven't though about them in ages, or never gave them a shot for being &quot;traditional&quot; during the post OGL-bust anti-traditional design mindset.<br /> <br /> The whole reason why we call the OGL era a boom-bust one, is because things got bigger than they could ever really sustain. Things looked more popular, but aren't necessarily more enduring popular, because people were spending way more than was justified. Not reaching those heights again isn't dying, is living sustainably.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T16:36:38-07:00","id":1480701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480612-why-were-there-only-two-books-published-for-dark-ages-mage?p=1480700#post1480700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not a fan of V5 (or things I've heard about W5 and H5) but the WoD is not dying because I don't like an edition, and the RPG market conditions aren't what they were like during the Clinton economic boom (again, economics far beyond RPGs matter, the 90s were so big for niche luxury items aimed at relatively low price points because it was boom economy for the middle class that has never truly been recovered from after multiple globally impacting economic disasters over the last two decades).<br /> <br /> V5 isn't going to reclaim VtM's position as the second biggest RPG. The WoD brand is, however, in general, the best it's been in a long time. The new reality of the RPG market is, once you stop trying to be a D&amp;D killer or caring what D&amp;D can do with Hasbro's monetary backing, currently pretty good and lots of older games are getting revisits by people that haven't though about them in ages, or never gave them a shot for being &quot;traditional&quot; during the post OGL-bust anti-traditional design mindset.<br /> <br /> The whole reason why we call the OGL era a boom-bust one, is because things got bigger than they could ever really sustain. Things looked more popular, but aren't necessarily more enduring popular, because people were spending way more than was justified. Not reaching those heights again isn't dying, is living sustainably.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like WOD for the unique setting, so its nice that its in a comfortable place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T03:25:15-07:00","id":1480736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That isn't actually why but you do you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why did they cancel them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T13:25:03-07:00","id":1480759,"title":"","content":"To get back to DAM for a moment:<br /> <br /> It's also worth remembering that DAM was hugely disliked by the fans on release. The love it has now is a combination of people that held on to its concepts for decades, and people revisiting some of its mechanics later during the long lull between the end of Revised and M20. The two big reasons it wasn't actually popular at the time, which are still relevant to the published material even if fans have seen to addressing a lot of it, were:<br /> <br /> 1) The lack of canon groups that would be present in a European setting.<br /> <br /> 2) The Pillar system being too opaque to easily interpret what Pillars do what, let alone make your own Fellowships<br /> <br /> A lot of the shift in opinion around DAM is not that DAM + Grimoire are seen as some hidden masterpiece, but because of a decade of fans addressing those two failings enough people can enjoy the really positive mechanical designs (Foundations and a few other things) without the frustrations of taking the already hard to adjudicate rules and making it worse by having the Pillars have even less internal structure than the Spheres do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T17:14:45-07:00","id":1480780,"title":"","content":"Indeed. If we ever get any DAM20 material (and STV is an option here), I really hope that the above points get addressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T12:21:47-07:00","id":1480851,"title":"","content":"I got one Storyteller's Vault DAM book and I wanna do another when I get another good idea and have the time for it. I really like DA:M.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T16:25:02-07:00","id":1480883,"title":"","content":"It's a very good question, in fact, although I love my Mage The Sorcerer's Crusade (certainly one of the most beautiful books released by WW), I think Dark Ages Mage is perhaps my favorite book from the whole WoD. It made magic much more interesting as it's really so tied with paradigm, each different paradigms, etc. Much different from the way we normally see most people running mage the ascension, with magic being like x-men power and paradigms a distant concept. It's a real pity that we didn't see more of Dark Ages Mage. On a side note, I feel the need to also mention Dark Ages Fae, such a magnificent and gorgeous book. These three are probably my favorite books from WW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T22:56:44-07:00","id":1480933,"title":"","content":"I never have problems with people disregarding Focus in M20 (and tended not to have similar problems with paradigm in 2e or Rev). There's a whole box of tools in the books to make sure players that lean into such things are rewarded, and ones that don't fall behind. Pretty much every example of &quot;X-men&quot; like play conditions were the ST not using that toolkit (either on purpose or ignorance). All DAM does is force you to deal with it at a considerable amount of mental overhead.<br /> <br /> Foundations are good (but should be something more like Attainments in Awakening so they're more customizable), but the Pillars ruin the whole point of having a flexible magic system instead of each Class of casters having their own spell lists: not having to reinvent the wheel to come up with effect that fit the characters. The whole point of the Ars Magia/Ascension/Awakening lineage is that &quot;I set someone on fire,&quot; has one base mechanical method despite countless ways of going about it in-character.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T10:12:36-07:00","id":1480973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480612-why-were-there-only-two-books-published-for-dark-ages-mage?p=1480664#post1480664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why was there a cancellation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ian Watson posted about this some years back with a really interesting insider's view:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.enworld.org/threads/what-happened-with-vampire.352460/page-3#post-6289181\" target=\"_blank\">What happened with Vampire? | Page 3 | EN World | Dungeons &amp; Dragons | Tabletop Roleplaying Games</a><br /> <br /> Here's the text for those who don't want to follow the link:<br /> <br /> &quot;Here's the thing. Sales had been on a steady downward trend, and with the evolving metaplot, the line was increasingly hard to get into for newcomers. Products being released were more and more niche, since just about everything had already been covered in the previous 13 years. So they made the very risky decision to do the Time of Judgment and then introduce an entirely new World of Darkness: one with no metaplot and a toolbox approach, which would help avoid some of the previous issues.<br /> <br /> With the benefit of hindsight we can see that the cause was a sales slump industry-wide. Publishing in general, but RPGs in particular, were suffering. But that wasn't easy to see at the time. WW made their decision for entirely sensible reasons, they just happened to be wrong.<br /> <br /> As an example of the sales slump -- one of the few for which numbers were made public -- VTM's 1998 Limited Edition rulebook sold 10,000 copies, and many more unlimited editions. Six years later VTR's 2004 corebook, which only had the one version, sold 10,000 copies, and that was exciting enough that WW issued a press release. That's a huge change in such a short period of time. WW was hurting.<br /> <br /> But it means we get to play in two different WoDs. We get to explore two different interpretations of werewolves, of changelings, of vampires, of demons. We get to introduce new weird stuff like Sin-Eaters and Prometheans. It's very freeing, creatively speaking. Both WoDs have their fans (and many are fans of both).&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}